<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/cursor') %>
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>

  <!-- Creucast -->
  <section class="creucast-section">
    <div class="creucast-bg-photo" style="background-image: url('/images/creucast.jpg');"></div>
    <div class="creucast-bg-overlay"></div>

    <div class="creucast-inner">
      <span class="creucast-brand reveal">Creucast</span>
      <h1 class="creucast-headline reveal reveal-delay-1">Building a creator collective</h1>
      <p class="creucast-subhead reveal reveal-delay-1">8 creators. Each gets a monthly content day, the rest of the group crews for you.</p>
      <p class="creucast-body reveal reveal-delay-2">We've got 4 spots left, on a 6-month commitment with proper structure behind it.</p>

      <p class="creucast-body reveal reveal-delay-2">Creators are becoming more valuable to mainstream TV than ever. Broadcasters want the loyal following that creators already know how to build &mdash; and that's exactly what you'll learn here. Every content day is a chance to grow it properly on YouTube, while picking up new skills and sharpening your craft alongside a group of other creators doing the same thing.</p>

      <div class="creucast-features reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="creucast-feature">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <path d="M4 8C4 6.89543 4.89543 6 6 6H8.5L9.5 4.5H14.5L15.5 6H18C19.1046 6 20 6.89543 20 8V17C20 18.1046 19.1046 19 18 19H6C4.89543 19 4 18.1046 4 17V8Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            <circle cx="12" cy="12.5" r="3.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          </svg>
          <span>Monthly content day</span>
        </div>
        <div class="creucast-feature">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <circle cx="8.5" cy="8" r="2.75" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <circle cx="16" cy="9" r="2.25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <path d="M3.5 18.5C3.5 15.7386 5.73858 13.5 8.5 13.5C11.2614 13.5 13.5 15.7386 13.5 18.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <path d="M14.5 14C17.0281 14.1633 19 16.2028 19 18.7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
          <span>Crew for each other</span>
        </div>
        <div class="creucast-feature">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <path d="M8.5 13.8L7 20L12 17.5L17 20L15.5 13.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <span>Production credit every month</span>
        </div>
        <div class="creucast-feature">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <rect x="4" y="5.5" width="16" height="14.5" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <path d="M4 9.5H20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
            <path d="M8 3.5V7M16 3.5V7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <path d="M8 13L10.5 15.5L16 10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <span>6-month structure</span>
        </div>
        <div class="creucast-feature">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <path d="M4 16L9 10L13 13L20 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            <path d="M14 5H20V11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <span>Grow YouTube audience</span>
        </div>
        <div class="creucast-feature">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <path d="M4 6.5C4 6.5 7 5 12 5C17 5 20 6.5 20 6.5V17.5C20 17.5 17 16 12 16C7 16 4 17.5 4 17.5V6.5Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            <path d="M12 5V16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          </svg>
          <span>Learn from each other</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="creucast-conditions reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <h2 class="creucast-conditions-title">What's Expected</h2>
        <ul class="creucast-conditions-list">
          <li>Your own YouTube channel, created and starting to post &mdash; or still in the early stages</li>
          <li>A production skill you bring to the table &mdash; camera, sound, lighting, editing, directing, hair &amp; makeup &mdash; or a plan to learn one in your first 2 months</li>
          <li>Available for your own monthly content day, and to crew for the others</li>
          <li>Show up to the weekly planning session for whichever member's day is up</li>
          <li>Based in Scotland</li>
          <li>First 2 months are a trial for everyone &mdash; no penalty either way if it's not a fit</li>
          <li>After the trial, 28 days' notice if you want to leave</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="creucast-faq reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <h2 class="creucast-faq-title">Common Questions</h2>
        <div class="creucast-faq-list">
          <div class="creucast-faq-item">
            <button class="creucast-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              Do I need to buy my own kit?
              <span class="creucast-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="creucast-faq-answer">
              <p>No. Everyone brings what they've got, and nobody's expected to buy gear to join. If a shoot needs something extra &mdash; a lens hire, a location fee, a lighting rig &mdash; that's covered by whoever's hero day it is, unless the group agrees in advance to split it. There's no shared budget or subscription; if shared kit ever makes sense, that's a conversation for further down the line, not a day-one requirement.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="creucast-faq-item">
            <button class="creucast-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              Who owns the footage, and where does it live?
              <span class="creucast-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="creucast-faq-answer">
              <p>You own and store your own raw footage from your hero day. In practice, that means transferring footage off crew members' cards or drives by the end of the shoot day, or within 48 hours, so nobody's chasing files a week later. There's no central shared drive &mdash; not needed at 8 people.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="creucast-faq-item">
            <button class="creucast-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              What happens if there's a disagreement within the group?
              <span class="creucast-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="creucast-faq-answer">
              <p>Keep it simple: raise it directly with the person first if it's something minor, like a missed crew day or a communication mix-up. If it's unresolved, or it's more serious &mdash; repeated no-shows, a conduct issue &mdash; it goes to the monthly review, or straight to the founder for a final call.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="creucast-faq-item">
            <button class="creucast-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              Are there any rules on what can be filmed or published?
              <span class="creucast-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="creucast-faq-answer">
              <p>Loose, but real. Nothing illegal, nothing that could reasonably be seen as discriminatory or that brings the group into disrepute, and no promotion of alcohol or drugs &mdash; some members will be building health, wellness, or sport-focused channels where that clashes badly. Outside of that, your own channel keeps full creative freedom. These guardrails only apply to what's filmed or published under the Creucast name, or in joint content.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="creucast-faq-item">
            <button class="creucast-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              Will the collective grow beyond 8 members?
              <span class="creucast-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="creucast-faq-answer">
              <p>Not for this first 6-month term &mdash; it stays capped at 8. We're not committing to a second cohort yet; the priority is proving the model works at this size before scaling it up. That's a conversation for the 6-month review.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="creucast-faq-item">
            <button class="creucast-faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              What about insurance and liability?
              <span class="creucast-faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="creucast-faq-answer">
              <p>Each member is responsible for their own kit and their own conduct on set. Creucast doesn't insure anyone's equipment or cover injury. If a location needs public liability insurance, that's arranged by whoever's hero day it is, not covered by a blanket Creucast policy.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <a href="/creucast/apply" class="creucast-cta reveal reveal-delay-2">Apply Now</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
  <%- include('partials/scripts') %>
</body>
</html>
